# The Drone ID plugin asks once, as the C# does (found 2026-10-04 on tridge's Mac: it asked at every
# start). OpenDroneID_Plugin's forceSettings shows "Restart Mission Planner to enable Drone ID Tab"
# when `tabcontrolactions` is unset, and saves the flight screen's pages and the settings so that the
# next start finds it set (Plugins/OpenDroneID2/OpenDroneID_Plugin.cs:66-79, GCSViews/FlightData.cs:
# 4746-4756). Here on a real first start - a config without the setting - the question comes; it is
# answered, the window closed by its close box and the planner started again on the same settings:
# no question the second time, and the plugin running.
# The built-in plugins: the runner leaves them out unless a script asks for them. The config's
# empty `DisabledPlugins` turns Open Drone ID on, off until a user does (the owner, 2026-10-05).
env MP_BUILTIN_PLUGINS 1
screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 30
env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK
env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
setup printf '<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><Config><DisabledPlugins></DisabledPlugins></Config>' > "$WORK/config.xml"
within 10
expect plugins.question ~ Restart Mission Planner to enable Drone ID Tab
click plugin-question-ok
expect plugins.question none
restart
settle 2
within 10
expect plugins.Open_Drone_ID.state running
expect plugins.question none
# The setting the answer saved does not name the page, so the strip does not have it, as in the
# C#; the tabs' Customize lists it.
expect fly.tabs.all ~ tabDroneID
expect plugins.forms.floating none
